.TH "GMB" "1" "Sep 2026" "GlassMarble 0.1.0" "GlassMarble Manual"

.SH NAME
gmb-memory - Query the developer memory: what do we know, when did it change, and why


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb memory [query] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the developer memory (.glassmarble/memory/) and answers
questions like "what do we know about Redis?" and "why was PaymentService added?".

.PP
Corrections never modify the underlying memory: they are an auditable
overlay applied to query results. Reasons are never invented: claims are
labelled by how they were established (FACT / EXPLICIT_REASON / INFERENCE
/ SPECULATION).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--ask\fP=""
	Ask the memory a question (deterministic retrieval, no LLM)

.PP
\fB--author\fP=""
	Who made the correction (audit trail, optional)

.PP
\fB--component\fP=""
	Show the full history of one component (substring match)

.PP
\fB--correct\fP=""
	Record a developer correction for a memory item (target ID or component name)

.PP
\fB--corrections\fP[=false]
	List the correction audit log instead of querying

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for memory

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Emit machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--kind\fP="INTENT"
	Correction kind: INTENT, LABEL, STATE, CONFIDENCE, REJECT, ACCEPT (used with --correct)

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Why the correction was made (audit trail)

.PP
\fB--value\fP=""
	The corrected value (required for INTENT, LABEL, STATE, CONFIDENCE; ignored for REJECT/ACCEPT)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dir\fP=""
	Target repository directory for analysis and queries

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Display developer memory overview and component summary
  gmb memory

  # Query developer memory for a specific topic or architectural concept
  gmb memory "why was the auth token cache introduced?"

  # Inspect longitudinal history of a specific component
  gmb memory --component payment

  # Record a developer convention correction
  gmb memory --correct auth --kind STATE --value active --reason "Migrated to production"

  # List the append-only developer correction audit trail
  gmb memory --corrections

  # Output memory query results as JSON
  gmb memory "database" --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgmb(1)\fP


